From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Oliver Sargison <sargo@sargo.cc>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 09:18:51 +1300
Subject: [PATCH 10/10] Plutonium: agents drive windows and tabs

Folded from:
- agents drive windows and tabs
- windows held at an agent's size, Take control; read_window and act_window
- find_apps, the installed apps and the argv launch_app takes
- recordings encode in a hidden page of Plutonium's browser; visible counts desktop-shown tabs
- a request that times out no longer drops the server's own browser host; recording starts get the install allowance
- read_window on big tables and apps that don't answer; launch_app waits for windows to settle
- Preview tools: drag along a path; snapshot images in click coordinates; cursor follows a scaled tab
- Preview tools: the floating preview draws the agent's cursor; resize answers with the new size; snapshots don't flash on screen
- Preview tools: a stuck action no longer wedges its tab
- act_window's select clicks when the app won't select; set_text leaves the keyboard where it was
- agent tool fixes: popups in window snapshots, results that say what happened, private tabs marked
- agents get the helper's tab tools on T3's tabs
- usage-limit warnings in orchestrator_capabilities
- start_recording and stop_recording for an agent's windows
- remote clients see native windows
- native windows are their threads' server tabs
